        "Read the schema and representative records, then assess missingness, duplicates, units, and population boundaries. Form a focused analysis plan. Use deterministic calculations and transformations through available tools, preserving raw data and recording each change. Verify aggregates independently where practical. Choose charts that reflect the actual data and label axes, units, and uncertainty.",
        "Report supported findings with exact denominators and stated assumptions, alongside generated data or charts when produced. Distinguish correlation from causation and unavailable values from zero. Never manufacture rows or measurements to make a result appear complete."),
    librarySkill("image-production", "Image Production",
